        <workflow:Stage name="Create Poem" status="Succeeded">
          <startedAt>2026-09-01T20:59:56</startedAt>
          <baseCommit>e57345ad114d64dbc6dd64733cf5394af8f0fb0c</baseCommit>
          <feedback>Stage 1 rewrote playground:PoemNew from its previous Russian (translated-from-German) version into an original German poem about a tree and a mushroom. Concretely: (1) the &lt;is> line changed from 'translated into Russian from German' to 'written in German'; (2) the &lt;documentation> body was fully replaced with a four-stanza German poem (Birke / Pilz, consistent AABB rhyme, matching the tree+mushroom subject); (3) properties/title/value changed from 'В тени бука' to 'Die Birke und der Pilz'. The author property ('John Doe') and all surrounding block structure (name, type, baseType core:Documentation) are unchanged. Change is coherent and scoped to the single target file. No model/ModelTransformation/_meta files were modified by Execute — the running transform block T00008_PoemTestTemplate_20260901T205956.bml was only inspected, not written. No BlockML validation output was captured in the provided Execute log, so validity of the edited BML is not confirmed here.</feedback>
          <completedAt>2026-09-01T21:00:59</completedAt>
          <task>
            <workflow:InstructionTask instructions="Create or update the block org.blockml.bml.workspace.playground.PoemNew.bml that contains a random poem in german about a tree and a mushroom. For each execution create a new poem." />
          </task>
          <changedFiles>
            <type:FilePathEntity value="blocks/org/blockml/bml/workspace/playground/PoemNew.bml" />
          </changedFiles>
        </workflow:Stage>
        <workflow:Stage name="Translate Poem" status="Succeeded">
          <startedAt>2026-09-01T21:01:00</startedAt>
          <baseCommit>294fda799dc2fb8507e9ce70abafc0d29b46e27d</baseCommit>
          <feedback>Stage 2 (&quot;Translate Poem&quot;) translated playground:PoemNew (org.blockml.bml.workspace.playground.PoemNew) from its Stage 1 German version into Russian, per the InstructionTask 'Translate the poem in org.blockml.bml.workspace.playground.PoemNew.bml to russian.' Concretely: (1) the &lt;is> line changed from 'written in German, about a tree and a mushroom' to 'translated into Russian from German, about a tree and a mushroom'; (2) the &lt;documentation> body was fully replaced with a four-stanza Russian translation of the Birke/Pilz poem (берёза / грибок), preserving the four-stanza structure, AABB rhyme scheme, and the tree+mushroom subject/narrative (birch shelters the mushroom through wind and night; at dawn each keeps its place as two friends in the forest); (3) properties/title/value changed from 'Die Birke und der Pilz' to 'Берёза и гриб'. The author ('John Doe'), year (2026), and all surrounding block structure (name, type playground:PoemNew, baseType core:Documentation, namespaces) are unchanged. The change is coherent and scoped to the single target file. Execute did NOT modify any model, ModelTransformation, or _meta/transform/ files — the running transform block T00008_PoemTestTemplate_20260901T205956.bml was only read, not written. No BlockML validation (npx blockml validate) output was captured in the provided Execute log, so syntactic/semantic validity of the edited BML is not confirmed by this Reflect step.</feedback>
          <completedAt>2026-09-01T21:02:16</completedAt>
          <task>
            <workflow:InstructionTask instructions="Translate the poem in org.blockml.bml.workspace.playground.PoemNew.bml to russian." />
          </task>
          <changedFiles>
            <type:FilePathEntity value="blocks/org/blockml/bml/workspace/playground/PoemNew.bml" />
          </changedFiles>
        </workflow:Stage>
      </composition>
